---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Trip Examples',href:'/trip-examples/'}];
const examples=[
 {type:'Hiking club',title:'Supported Multi-Day Trekking',image:images.trekking,summary:'Route difficulty, lodging, luggage support, preparation, and contingency built around a hiking community.',href:'/group-travel/hiking-clubs/'},
 {type:'Dive community',title:'Beginner Learn-to-Scuba Week',image:images.water,summary:'Training progression, accommodation, transfers, equipment, recovery, and non-diving time planned together.',href:'/learn-to-trips/scuba-diving/'},
 {type:'Wellness community',title:'Active-Rest Group Journey',image:images.lake,summary:'Movement, culture, comfortable lodging, recovery, and shared time without turning the trip into a performance program.',href:'/group-travel/wellness-yoga/'},
 {type:'Business or team',title:'Experience-Led Team Travel',image:images.city,summary:'A real destination purpose, selected shared activities, strong meals, optional work time, and room for genuine conversation.',href:'/group-travel/businesses-teams/'},
 {type:'Social group',title:'Hosted Culture & Cruise Program',image:images.boat,summary:'Cruise or cultural travel with group arrival planning, shared experiences, optionality, and coordinated pre/post travel.',href:'/cultural-cruise-travel/hosted-cruises/'},
 {type:'Private group',title:'First Active Trip for Friends',image:images.coast,summary:'Shorter active days, clear difficulty, comfortable recovery, optional extensions, and preparation for mixed experience levels.',href:'/private-group-travel/'}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Group Trip Planning Examples | Talon Expeditions" description="Representative group trip planning examples for hiking clubs, dive communities, wellness groups, teams, social groups, and private travelers considering supported travel with Talon Expeditions." image={images.trekking} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="av-inner-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.trekking}')`}><div class="shell"><h1>Trip Planning Examples</h1><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="av-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Representative Planning Scenarios</p><h2>See How the Planning Model Changes With the Group</h2></div><p>These examples illustrate planning logic rather than advertise fictional departures. Two organizations visiting the same destination can need completely different travel structures because their people, purpose, activity, support, and budget assumptions differ.</p><a class="button button-small" href="/plan-a-trip/">Build Your Own Trip</a></div><div class="av-destination-grid">{examples.map((item)=><a class="av-destination-card" href={item.href} style={`background-image:url('${item.image}')`}><div class="av-destination-card-top"><span>{item.type}</span><span class="av-card-arrow">↗</span></div><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.summary}</p><div class="av-destination-tags"><span>Planning example</span><span>Private group</span></div></a>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="av-proof-band" style={`background-image:url('${images.planning}')`}><div class="shell"><div class="av-proof-head"><p class="eyebrow">What Stays Consistent</p><h2>The itinerary changes. The planning discipline does not.</h2></div><div class="av-proof-grid"><div class="av-proof-card"><h3>Who Is Traveling?</h3><p>Group size, experience, activity, rooming, origin cities, budget sensitivity, and why these people want to travel together.</p><small>Traveler profile</small></div><div class="av-proof-card"><h3>What Is the Trip For?</h3><p>A route, a skill, a social program, a club objective, a team experience, or simply a more active way to experience a place.</p><small>Purpose</small></div><div class="av-proof-card"><h3>What Needs Support?</h3><p>Travel bookings, local operators, transfers, participant information, readiness, equipment, hosting, or a combination.</p><small>Scope</small></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="av-process"><div class="shell av-process-grid"><div class="av-process-visual" style={`background-image:url('${images.road}')`}><div class="av-process-callout"><h3>Replace the Assumptions With Your Real Group</h3><p>That is when a planning example becomes a useful itinerary.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Build From Reality</p><h2>Start With the Group and the Outcome</h2><p class="av-process-lead">Bring likely dates, destination ideas, activity interests, budget range, or simply the kind of experience you want people to have. The planning process can determine what trip structure is realistic from there.</p><div class="av-process-topline"><strong>Start a planning inquiry</strong><a href="/plan-a-trip/">↗</a></div><div class="av-process-steps"><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">◎</div><div><h3>People</h3><p>Who is actually likely to join?</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">⌖</div><div><h3>Purpose</h3><p>What should make this trip worth doing together?</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">▣</div><div><h3>Support</h3><p>Which moving parts should Talon coordinate?</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">✓</div><div><h3>Clarity</h3><p>What must participants understand before committing?</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
